spec:
  grid: 4-10 rows x 7-20 cols; output same size
  colors: exactly 3 — background (most frequent), obstacle (present on bottom row), moving (never on bottom row or in blocked cells)
  obstacle:
    structure: column-fill — each column is solid obstacle from some height down to bottom row
    floor_profile: 2-4 distinct heights forming a terrain; creates 1-5 pockets (contiguous column runs above min height)
    bottom_profile: bottom-heavy; usually most columns on the bottom row are obstacle, with rare sparse bottom-only post cases
    height_profile: occupied obstacle columns are low on average (about 1-3 cells); occasional taller columns may appear but must not dominate
    bottom_concentration: most obstacle pixels lie in the bottom three rows
    connectivity: 1-3 connected components (posts/walls can be separate)
    coverage: 8-52% of grid cells
  moving_objects:
    count: 1-3 per input (4-connected monochromatic components)
    size: 1-21 pixels; bbox 1-6 rows x 1-7 cols
    placement: each object fits within free (non-blocked) cells of a pocket; columns stay within pocket bounds
    initial_position: objects start in upper portion of grid, above blocked zone
    output_separation: after settling, no moving object pixel is 8-adjacent to any obstacle pixel
  blocked_zone: obstacle pixels + one-row cushion above each obstacle pixel + entire bottom row
  transform: |
    Drop all moving objects simultaneously under gravity (one row per step).
    An object moves down if its shifted shape hits no blocked cell and no other moving pixel.
    Repeat until no object can move. Objects preserve shape; columns unchanged.
    Objects may merge into fewer components after settling.
  non_triviality: at least one object drops >= 1 row; drop range 0-4 rows per object [observed]

